{"text": "NORTH COUNTY fp\n\nTRANSIT DISTRICT\n\n810 Mission Avenue\nOceanside, CA 92054\n\n(760) 966-6500\n\n(760) 967-2001 (fax)\nwww.GoNCTD.com\n\nBOARD OF DIRECTORS\n\nBill Horn\nSupervisor. County of San Diego\nBoord Chair\nMark Packard\nCounciimember, City of Carlsbad\nBoard Vice Chair\nDonald Mosier\nCouncilmember, City of De! Mar\n\nTony Kranz\nCouncilmember, City cf Encintas\n\nEd Gallo\nCouncilmember, City of Escondido\n\nGary Felien\nCouncilmember, City of Oceanside\n\nRebecca Jones\nCouncilmember, City of San Marcos\n\nMike Nichols\nMayor, City of Solena Beach\n\nJohn J. Aguilera\nCouncilmember, City of Vista\n\nEXECUTIVE DIRECTOR\nMathew O. Tucker\n\nGENERAL COUNSEL\nLori A. Winfree\n\nJuly 23, 2013\n\nMr. Brad Racino\n\nemailed to: bradracino@gmail.com\n\n5500 Campanile Drive\nPSFA 361C\nSan Diego, CA 92182\n\nRe: Public Records Act Request dated July 11, 2013\n\nDear Mr. Racino:\n\nThis letter shall serve as North County Transit District's (\u2018NCTD\u201d) response to your\npublic records request dated July 8, 2013, which NCTD received via the on-line Public\nRecord Request system, and extended until July 23, 2013, requesting the following:\n\n1.\n\nA copy of Matt Tucker\u2019s resume as presented to the district when he was hired\nin late 2008. Please take note that with respect to job applications and\nresumes of public employees, the court in Eskaton Monterey Hospital v.\nMyers, 134 Cal. App. 3d 788, 794, 184 Cal Rptr. 840 (1982), said that\n\u201cinformation as to the education, training, experience, awards, previous\npositions and publications of the (employee)... is routinely presented in both\nprofessional and social settings, is relatively innocuous and implicates no\napplicable privacy or public policy exemption.\u201d If you choose to deny this\nrequest, please provide a written explanation for the denial including a\nreference to the specific statutory exemption(s) upon which you rely. Also,\nplease provide all segregable portions of otherwise exempt material.\n\nAfter conducting a search for records responsive to your request, NCTD has\ndetermined that your request seeks, in whole, records, which are exempt from\ndisclosure. The requested record is being withheld pursuant to Government Code\nsection 6254(c) as the requested record is maintained in a personnel file. The person\nresponsible for withholding the document is the undersigned. However, enclosed\nplease find Mr. Tucker's biographical summary page, which has previously been\nmade public.\n\nVira Villarreal\nManager of Administration",
